From: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
Date: Tue, 01 Sep 2026 09:28:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: mediatek: mt7986: set the ETDM slots and clock divider

The SDG voice boards drive a Silicon Labs SLIC on ETDM5 instead of an
audio codec. The SLIC frame carries four 16-bit slots. At 16 kHz the
wire frame sync must stay at 8 kHz. Two register fields did not follow
that need.

Slot count: mt7986_si3218x_init() programs four slots into
ETDM_OUT5_CON0. mtk_dai_etdm_config() derived the same field from
params_channels(), and the DAI limits a stream to two channels. A
stream then reprogrammed the bus to two slots. Set the field to the
four slots of the SLIC frame. Drop get_etdm_ch_fixup(); no caller
remains.

Clock divider: the SLIC packs one 16 kHz channel into two 16-bit
samples of one 8 kHz PCM frame. The AFE must move 16000 frames per
second while bit 12 of ETDM_OUT5_CON5 (ETDM_CLK_DIV) divides the wire
frame sync to 8 kHz. The vendor code wrote the bit for every rate.
Drive the field from params_rate() in the playback branch of
mtk_dai_etdm_config(), beside the other ETDM_OUT5 rate fields. That
branch runs on every hw_params for both directions, and no other site
writes the field. Without the clear, a 16 kHz close would leave the
divider set for the next 8 kHz open. A measurement on the SDG-8732v
confirmed the divided frame sync at 16 kHz.

The DAI sets symmetric_rate, so soc_pcm_params_symmetry() refuses a
second direction at a different rate with -EINVAL, and
soc_pcm_hw_clean() drops the stored rate only when the DAI active
count is one. A peer with hw_params therefore keeps the rate pinned.
At 8000 the field takes 0, its reset value; regmap drops the unchanged
write, so the 8 kHz register sequence does not change.

Known limitation: mt7986_si3218x_init() enables both ETDM directions
at probe, and the OUT5 setup fields land before this field. A first
change from 8 kHz to 16 kHz therefore shows a brief mixed geometry on
an enabled bus. The vendor flow already writes its configuration under
ETDM_EN; this change keeps that order.

Signed-off-by: Chad Monroe <chad@monroe.io>
---
 sound/soc/mediatek/mt7986/mt7986-dai-etdm.c |   34 ++++++++----------
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+), 18 deletions(-)

--- a/sound/soc/mediatek/mt7986/mt7986-dai-etdm.c
+++ b/sound/soc/mediatek/mt7986/mt7986-dai-etdm.c
@@ -146,20 +146,6 @@ static void mtk_dai_etdm_shutdown(struct
 	clk_bulk_disable_unprepare(afe_priv->num_clks, afe_priv->clks);
 }
 
-static unsigned int get_etdm_ch_fixup(unsigned int channels)
-{
-	if (channels > 16)
-		return 24;
-	else if (channels > 8)
-		return 16;
-	else if (channels > 4)
-		return 8;
-	else if (channels > 2)
-		return 4;
-	else
-		return 2;
-}
-
 static int mtk_dai_etdm_config(struct mtk_base_afe *afe,
 			       struct snd_pcm_hw_params *params,
 			       struct snd_soc_dai *dai,
@@ -170,7 +156,6 @@ static int mtk_dai_etdm_config(struct mt
 	unsigned int rate = params_rate(params);
 	unsigned int etdm_rate = mt7986_etdm_rate_transform(afe->dev, rate);
 	unsigned int afe_rate = mt7986_afe_rate_transform(afe->dev, rate);
-	unsigned int channels = params_channels(params);
 	unsigned int bit_width = params_width(params);
 	unsigned int wlen = get_etdm_wlen(bit_width);
 	unsigned int val = 0;
@@ -187,7 +172,12 @@ static int mtk_dai_etdm_config(struct mt
 	mask |= ETDM_FMT_MASK;
 	val |= FIELD_PREP(ETDM_FMT_MASK, etdm_data->format);
 	mask |= ETDM_CH_NUM_MASK;
-	val |= FIELD_PREP(ETDM_CH_NUM_MASK, get_etdm_ch_fixup(channels) - 1);
+	/*
+	 * The ETDM frame always carries the four SLIC time slots that
+	 * mt7986_si3218x_init() programs into ETDM_OUT5_CON0, so the
+	 * slot count does not follow the ALSA channel count.
+	 */
+	val |= FIELD_PREP(ETDM_CH_NUM_MASK, 4 - 1);
 	mask |= RELATCH_SRC_MASK;
 	val |= FIELD_PREP(RELATCH_SRC_MASK, APLL_CLK);
 
@@ -204,9 +194,17 @@ static int mtk_dai_etdm_config(struct mt
 		regmap_update_bits(afe->regmap, ETDM_OUT5_CON4,
 				   OUT_SEL_FS_MASK, OUT_SEL_FS(etdm_rate));
 
-		/* set ETDM_OUT5_CON5 */
+		/*
+		 * The SLIC packs one 16 kHz channel into two 16-bit samples
+		 * of a single 8 kHz PCM frame. The wire frame sync must stay
+		 * at 8 kHz while the AFE moves 16000 frames per second.
+		 * Clear the field at every other rate, because no other site
+		 * in the tree writes it. A 16 kHz close would otherwise leave
+		 * the divider on for the next 8 kHz open.
+		 */
 		regmap_update_bits(afe->regmap, ETDM_OUT5_CON5,
-				   ETDM_CLK_DIV_MASK, ETDM_CLK_DIV);
+				   ETDM_CLK_DIV_MASK,
+				   rate == 16000 ? ETDM_CLK_DIV : 0);
 		break;
 	case SNDRV_PCM_STREAM_CAPTURE:
 		/* set ETDM_IN5_CON0 */
